# Secrets manifest — {{PRODUCT_NAME}}

> Index of every secret: name, what uses it, scope, and home. **No values here.**
> Values live in `secrets/secrets.local.env` (gitignored) and are synced to
> GitHub Actions for CI-scoped ones via `bin/secrets-sync.sh`.

| Name | Used by | Scope | Home | Set? |
| ---- | ------- | ----- | ---- | ---- |
| `SUPABASE_URL` | web+mobile build | CI/runtime | GitHub Actions | ☐ |
| `SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` | web+mobile build | CI/runtime | GitHub Actions | ☐ |
| `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` | web deploy | CI/runtime | GitHub Actions | ☐ |
| `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` | web deploy | CI/runtime | GitHub Actions | ☐ |
| `FIREBASE_APP_ID` | mobile deploy | CI/runtime | GitHub Actions | ☐ |
| `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` | mobile deploy | CI/runtime | GitHub Actions | ☐ |
| `GITHUB_PAT` | GitHub MCP | local MCP | shell/keychain | ☐ |
| `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` | Supabase MCP | local MCP | shell/keychain | ☐ |
| `SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF` | Supabase MCP (project) | local MCP | shell/keychain | ☐ |
| `STITCH_API_KEY` | Stitch MCP (if used) | local MCP | shell/keychain | ☐ |
| `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` | Stripe MCP/worker (if used) | local MCP + Worker | shell + wrangler secret | ☐ |
| `E2E_TEST_EMAIL` | Playwright auth | test | local mirror (+ Actions if CI e2e) | ☐ |
| `E2E_TEST_PASSWORD` | Playwright auth | test | local mirror (+ Actions if CI e2e) | ☐ |

Legend: **CI/runtime** → only in GitHub Actions (write via `gh secret set`, never
read back). **local MCP** → only in your machine's shell/keychain. **test** →
staging-only credentials.
